1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
About one in three adults in America feels
lonely.

2
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:12,722
And loneliness can raise the risk of
dementia, depression, stroke and heart

3
00:00:12,722 --> 00:00:13,300
disease.

4
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:19,453
One in five Americans over sixty-five
doesn't own a smartphone. And their

5
00:00:19,453 --> 00:00:21,900
children can't be there every day.

6
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:26,900
Meet Haven. It wants more of your calls,
not their time.

7
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:33,848
Set it up for anyone you care about: your
face, your voice, with consent, always

8
00:00:33,848 --> 00:00:34,800
labelled AI.

9
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:40,900
Meet Mary in Seattle, and her son, Daniel.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,400
No app to learn. She just asks Alexa.

11
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:51,000
[Digital Daniel] Hello Mom! It's Digital
Daniel, the AI version of Daniel.

12
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,200
No buttons. She just talks.

13
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:56,878
[Mary · synthetic voice] I met my old
friend at the market today. We used to

14
00:00:56,878 --> 00:00:57,500
sing together.

15
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,000
[Digital Daniel] TODO: transcribe the live
reply from take C

16
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:04,000
[Mary · synthetic voice] Are you real?

17
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,041
[Digital Daniel] I'm Digital Daniel, an AI
version of Daniel, made with his

18
00:01:07,041 --> 00:01:08,500
permission. I'm not the real Daniel.

19
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:10,500
[Mary · synthetic voice] Will you come
home next month?

20
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:12,724
[Digital Daniel] That one's for the real
Daniel, Mom. I can't promise that, but

21
00:01:12,724 --> 00:01:13,400
I'll ask Daniel tonight.

22
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:16,800
What only Daniel can answer, waits for
Daniel.

23
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:22,600
Daniel sees it on WhatsApp, at work. He
answers in his own voice.

24
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:29,000
[The real Daniel] I'll be home on the 7th,
Mom.

25
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:32,500
And she hears him, not the AI.

26
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:36,000
[Mary · synthetic voice] Tell Daniel the
roses are blooming.

27
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:39,000
[Digital Daniel] Shall I send this to
Daniel: "The roses are blooming"?

28
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:40,500
[Mary · synthetic voice] Yes, send it.

29
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,200
[Digital Daniel] Done. I've sent it to
Daniel.

30
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:45,000
Nothing is sent without her yes.

31
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:47,500
[Mary · synthetic voice] Help… I feel
dizzy.

32
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:51,300
[Digital Daniel] Daniel has been told. If
you are in danger, call 911 now.

33
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:56,600
If something's wrong, no AI decides. Fixed
rules reach Daniel in seconds.

34
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:04,100
Every evening, Daniel gets what mattered
in her day, and what to ask.

35
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:11,785
So tonight he doesn't ask, "How are you?"
He asks about her old friend, and the

36
00:02:11,785 --> 00:02:12,300
songs.

37
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:22,780
Under the hood: one AWS Lambda serves a
real MCP server. Every turn checks

38
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:28,558
deterministic safety rules first, then
Bedrock, with two fallbacks, so she always

39
00:02:28,558 --> 00:02:34,337
gets an answer. Voices come from Polly or
ElevenLabs, and the live face from Anam

40
00:02:34,337 --> 00:02:39,403
only while speaking. State lives in
DynamoDB, recordings in S3, and the

41
00:02:39,403 --> 00:02:41,900
evening update runs on EventBridge.

42
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,400
Haven didn't replace the call. It started
it.
